. *****************************************************************************
> ***
. ****************** Do-File for Hypothesis 4: Gender Attitude Analysis *******
> ****
. *****************************************************************************
> ***
. 
. * Changes from PAP
. * The variable "hgnrpers" denoting number of persons living in a household fr
> om the dataset "pgen" that was present in the documentation was unfortunately
>  not featured in the datasets made available to us, therefore we could not ca
> lculate the Nr of Adults control variable and consequently we dropped it from
>  the analyses. 
. * The variable pl:plh0308_v2 used for construction of GenderAttitude did not 
> have 0-7 response options as we originally outlined, but 1-7, so the code was
>  adjusted to reflect that. 
. * In addition to excluding respondents who report having their first child in
>  2018, we excluded also those having their first child any year after.
. * Recoded negative values for all control variables as missing values
. * When constructing HavingDaughter variable per Wave, we have counted with ki
> ds-related variables from the year prior (so HavingDaughters for 2005 runs ou
> r pre-defined construction formula with kids from before 2005)
. * EastWest: will we code East as 0 and West as 1, Immigration status: 0 = Ger
> man, 1 = Immigrant
. 
. * Authors: [REDACTED] & [REDACTED]
. 
. * ============================
. * Setup *
. * ============================
. 
. * clear all
. version 19.5

. set maxvar 10000


